{"title":"*Buckley: The Life and Revolution that Changed America*","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/921726485/0/marginalrevolution~Buckley-The-Life-and-Revolution-that-Changed-America.html","date":1752648617000,"content":"<p><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Buckley-Life-Revolution-Changed-America/dp/0375502343/ref=sr_1_1?crid=2EE8YIN2NQSV0&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.SjdfjjXbM8r3Ly5mh17eslgQqZdswVArhThE8nE5hQJQKqrnshmbDOcQfkcEXd9SQVoNgWaPNPijZ8knf2BWRFN5glsDNmi0122EKsBT4JFpvN3PqJkv9T83dPoGa_nqxMNNNuXWXC_0NkXdOzBu_Z0HajMpp0mPwdg0rR7Je6dyP8qsaIKmOhu31XgzSyXvlfDFnzLtlwrWLe7HGcIb2gE4921ivFSMvX3IAPiGh1s.WHQauvLeJsDQrgTCA99JC9lwr4TBj8FebrHeifFTElE&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=sam+tanenhaus+buckley&amp;qid=1752627364&amp;sprefix=sam+tanen%2Caps%2C111&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">By Sam Tanenhaus</a>.  I held off reading this book at first, as I felt I already knew a lot about Buckley and his life.  But it is excellent.  Very well written and engaging throughout.  I learned a good deal, and it is one of the best books on the history of the American 20th century right wing.</p>\r\n<p>As a youth, watching <em>Firing Line</em>, I frequently was frustrated that Buckley was not more analytical, and that he sometimes spoke in such a roundabout manner.  In part I wanted to expand Conversations with Tyler to fill that gap.  I am also indebted to Buckley for first getting me interested in Bach.  So he played a very definite role in my life.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/07/buckley-the-life-and-revolution-that-changed-america.html\">*Buckley: The Life and Revolution that Changed America*</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/921726485/0/margi